+`fly_auto.py` uploads a mission, arms in AUTO and checks every waypoint, the
+cross-track error on each leg, the attitude and the end: the rover drives a
+20 m square back to home; the plane takes off north from the runway, flies a
+400 x 200 m circuit at 50 m, approaches from the south and lands. Both FMUs
+start facing north, so use home heading 0.
